{{- /* top-level helmfile fields that ATLAS doesn't own
     should pass through to the emitted state file unchanged.

     The user's app template can declare:
       - repositories  : helm chart repo registrations needed by releases
       - helmDefaults  : default options for every release in this state
       - templates     : yaml-anchor-style shared release config blocks
       - bases         : nested helmfile imports
       - hooks         : pre/post-event commands

     ATLAS owns environments, commonLabels, and releases — those get
     rewritten by helmfile.instance. Everything else must reach helmfile
     verbatim or the user's chart resolution / defaults / hook wiring
     silently breaks.

     We assert pass-through via helmDefaults because it's a data-only
     block that helmfile won't try to dereference during `build`.
     `repositories:` would also pass through (same one-line emission
     change covers every top-level key) but asserting it would require
     helmfile to call `helm repo add` against the listed URL, which
     fetches index.yaml — a fake URL hangs the test on DNS, a real URL
     introduces network flakiness. helmDefaults exercises the same code
     path without either failure mode. */ -}}
helmDefaults:
  timeout: 123
  wait: false
releases:
  - name: stage3-passthrough
    chart: ../../charts/chart1
    namespace: test
